NAME
    nano - full-screen terminal text editor

SYNOPSIS
    nano <path>

DESCRIPTION
    Shipped external DianaSh program providing a minimal full-screen
    text editor for creating and editing files inside the shell sandbox.
    If <path> does not exist yet, it is created when saved. Saved files
    always use LF ('\n') line endings.

    nano requires an interactive terminal for both standard input and
    standard output, and exits with an error when input or output is
    redirected or when run in a non-terminal console.

    Supported keys:

    Up, Down, Left, Right   Move cursor (Left/Right wrap across lines).
    Home, End               Jump to start or end of the current line.
    PageUp, PageDown        Scroll up or down by one screen page.
    Enter                   Insert a newline at the cursor.
    Backspace, Delete       Delete character before or at the cursor.
    Ctrl-O                  Save the buffer to <path>.
    Ctrl-X                  Exit (prompts to save if modified; y, n, or
                            Esc to cancel).

EXAMPLES
    nano /Logs/setup.sh

EXIT STATUS
    0   Editor exited normally (whether saved or not).
    1   Missing path, path outside DIANASH_ROOT sandbox, non-terminal
        environment, or file read error.

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), source(1), export(1), dianash(1)
